1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:03,420
Now, let me start by asking you, Sebas,

2
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:08,730
do I need to explain to you
what I am doing here?

3
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:11,490
No, there is no need.

4
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:16,240
Is something the matter, Sebas?
You're sweating something awful.

5
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:18,870
I'll lend you my handkerchief.

6
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,550
I have brought her.

7
00:01:55,550 --> 00:02:01,140
Come on in, Tuare,
the human pet that Sebas took in.

8
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:06,390
You have courage to not run away.

9
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:17,740
--On your knees--
--No. Control spells are unnecessary.

10
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:21,910
To extol her courage,
I will permit her indecorum before me.

11
00:02:22,750 --> 00:02:26,950
First, why don't I tell you my name?
I am Ains Ooal Gown.

12
00:02:26,950 --> 00:02:29,540
I am the master of Sebas over there.

13
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:31,040
R-Right.

14
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:34,960
Now then, Sebas, I thought
I instructed you to act in a way

15
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:37,050
that would not draw attention.

16
00:02:37,050 --> 00:02:37,810
Yes, my lord.

17
00:02:37,810 --> 00:02:42,310
Nonetheless, you have courted trouble
for the sake of this no-account woman.

18
00:02:42,310 --> 00:02:43,260
Am I wrong?

19
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:48,680
I am deeply sorry that my indiscretion
has earned your displeasure, Lord Ains,

20
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:52,190
and I will be more than mindful that
something like this never happens again.

21
00:02:52,190 --> 00:02:55,480
Enough. Everyone makes mistakes.

22
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:59,700
Sebas, I will forgive your trivial blunder.

23
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:02,340
Lord Ains, I am most grateful.

24
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:06,450
However! You must
make amends for your mistake.

25
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:08,040
Kill her.

26
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:11,400
What... did you say?

27
00:03:12,110 --> 00:03:18,090
Sebas, are you a dog that obeys
the Supreme One-- that obeys the 41?

28
00:03:18,090 --> 00:03:21,060
Or are you someone
who believes his own will is correct?

29
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:23,300
--Well, I--
--You need not answer!

30
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:26,060
Demonstrate it to me through results.

31
00:03:47,950 --> 00:03:49,120
What are you...?!

32
00:03:51,370 --> 00:03:52,870
Sebas, back away!

33
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:53,810
Yes, my lord.

34
00:03:55,380 --> 00:04:01,050
Cocytus, was that attack undeniably
and deliberately intended to kill her?

35
00:04:01,050 --> 00:04:03,130
Without a doubt.

36
00:04:03,390 --> 00:04:08,640
In that case, I take it as proof
that Sebas's loyalty is unfeigned.

37
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:10,890
Good work, Sebas.

38
00:04:10,890 --> 00:04:11,680
Yes, my lord.

39
00:04:13,770 --> 00:04:16,240
Now, let's move on to the next topic.

40
00:04:16,830 --> 00:04:21,690
Sebas, I have evaluated that your work here
has gathered enough information.

41
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:25,660
I have decided that we will vacate the mansion,
and withdraw to Nazarick.

42
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:28,800
As for the fate of the woman,
give me some time.

43
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:33,120
I do not think it will be death, but know
that this determination is not absolute.

44
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:36,580
Demiurge, I will be taking Victim back with me.

45
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:37,300
Right.

46
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:41,050
Greater Teleportation!

47
00:04:45,930 --> 00:04:51,060
She appears to be fatigued.
I will let her get some rest in her room.

48
00:04:51,060 --> 00:04:57,310
I will take her there. This is no longer
a matter. Am I right, Lord Demiurge?

49
00:04:57,310 --> 00:05:00,340
I suppose. You are correct, Sebas.

50
00:05:05,690 --> 00:05:08,050
I have no intention of apologizing.

51
00:05:09,070 --> 00:05:12,410
However, if I had
gone about this some other way,

52
00:05:12,410 --> 00:05:15,330
things would not have ended up this way.

53
00:05:15,330 --> 00:05:16,830
Lord Sebas...

54
00:05:16,830 --> 00:05:19,990
You go and live happily in the world of humans.

55
00:05:20,540 --> 00:05:23,800
Lord Ains should be able
to perform memory manipulation.

56
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:27,840
Erase all of your bad memories, and live.

57
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:29,720
What about you, Lord Sebas?

58
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:32,470
Let's have him erase
your memories of me, as well.

59
00:05:32,470 --> 00:05:35,180
There is nothing good
to remember about me, after all.

60
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:37,270
What do you mean, nothing good?

61
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:42,360
My happiness comes from
being with you, Lord Sebas!

62
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:45,190
I do not think of this place as hell.

63
00:05:45,190 --> 00:05:49,870
You gave me meals to fill my belly,
and a decent job to do.

64
00:05:49,870 --> 00:05:53,370
I was born and raised in a small village.

65
00:05:53,370 --> 00:05:56,110
My life there was a difficult one, as well.

66
00:05:56,670 --> 00:06:00,040
Even after plowing the fields
while our tummies were grumbling,

67
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:03,720
the feudal lord took away
most of the crops that grew,

68
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:06,380
leaving next to nothing
to go into our own mouths.

69
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:11,150
Not to mention that in our lord's view,
we were simply playthings.

70
00:06:11,670 --> 00:06:15,220
Even when I screamed,
he would keep laughing as he violated me...

71
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:15,930
I...!

72
00:06:15,930 --> 00:06:17,180
All right.

73
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,480
It may mean your death.

74
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:23,250
If I am to be killed by you, Lord Sebas...

75
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,990
...by you, the gentleman
who offered me his warmth

76
00:06:25,990 --> 00:06:28,200
when I was destined to die back there...

77
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:34,540
Tuare, I will ask Lord Ains to let me
take you back with me to Nazarick.

78
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:36,410
Thank you very much.

79
00:06:36,410 --> 00:06:38,540
Let me verify one thing first.

80
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:41,540
Do you have any attachments
to the world of humans?

81
00:06:41,810 --> 00:06:46,260
I would... kind of like to see
my younger sister again.

82
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:51,050
But my desire not to remember
any of the past is stronger still.

83
00:06:51,050 --> 00:06:55,060
Very well. You go to your room.

84
00:06:55,060 --> 00:06:58,180
I will go and see Lord Ains again.

85
00:06:58,180 --> 00:06:59,230
Okay.

86
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:12,990
That was prickly.

87
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:18,560
I've never shared a happy kiss before.

88
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:23,130
I have returned.

89
00:07:23,130 --> 00:07:25,880
Is something the matter? Your face is flushed.

90
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:29,130
It is nothing, Lord Demiurge.

91
00:07:29,130 --> 00:07:31,500
You need not use that title with me.

92
00:07:32,010 --> 00:07:33,610
I don't need it, either.

93
00:07:33,930 --> 00:07:34,680
All right.

94
00:07:37,550 --> 00:07:40,290
Thank you for greeting me. Rise.

95
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:47,900
Now then, Demiurge, I trust your
anxious mind has now been satisfied?

96
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:51,780
I never once thought
that Sebas would betray me.

97
00:07:52,110 --> 00:07:54,070
I am terribly sorry for that.

98
00:07:54,070 --> 00:07:57,410
Further, I thank you so much
for acknowledging my viewpoint

99
00:07:57,410 --> 00:08:01,440
when I voiced my objection
to your decision, Lord Ains.

100
00:08:01,780 --> 00:08:04,830
It is no matter. I have oversights, as well.

101
00:08:04,830 --> 00:08:09,210
Now, you wished to discuss how to
deal with that human woman, Sebas?

102
00:08:09,210 --> 00:08:09,970
Yes, my lord.

103
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:13,220
You worry that after the woman is released,

104
00:08:13,220 --> 00:08:16,010
she could leak information
about Nazarick, is that it?

105
00:08:16,430 --> 00:08:18,310
Then after her memories are manipulated,

106
00:08:18,310 --> 00:08:21,310
you can give her some money
and leave her in a suitable place.

107
00:08:21,310 --> 00:08:25,560
Lord Ains, I believe that killing her
would be a more certain way.

108
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:30,570
Stop. I do not much like homicidal acts
when they gain me nothing.

109
00:08:30,570 --> 00:08:35,700
Understood. Well, shall I put her to work
at the stockyard that I oversee?

110
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:38,620
Ah, the one where you keep the chimeras?

111
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:39,740
Lord Ains...

112
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:41,620
Hmm? What is it, Sebas?

113
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:45,710
If you are willing, I was thinking that
I would like to put Tuare to work

114
00:08:45,710 --> 00:08:48,090
in the Great Tomb of Nazarick.

115
00:08:51,170 --> 00:08:54,550
I once asked the same thing of Cocytus,

116
00:08:54,550 --> 00:08:57,220
but Sebas, how would that benefit me?

117
00:08:57,220 --> 00:09:00,430
My lord, Tuare can prepare meals.

118
00:09:00,430 --> 00:09:03,350
There are only a few people
in Nazarick that can cook.

119
00:09:03,350 --> 00:09:06,980
I think it would be better
to have a few others who can cook.

120
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:11,150
Indeed, I, too, found that
a point bearing consideration.

121
00:09:11,150 --> 00:09:16,240
But can she prepare food
that is worthy of Nazarick?

122
00:09:17,910 --> 00:09:21,160
What Tuare can cook
appears to be household fare.

123
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:23,870
If you ask whether that is worthy of Nazarick...

124
00:09:23,870 --> 00:09:26,540
I do not think that
dishes such as steamed potatoes

125
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:28,630
should be served at Nazarick.

126
00:09:28,630 --> 00:09:32,710
I cannot help but wonder if your thinking
is too hasty, Lord Demiurge.

127
00:09:32,710 --> 00:09:37,720
If she can do home cooking,
she can also master other kinds of cooking.

128
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:40,140
We should look to the future.

129
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:44,930
In that case, I should like her to help out
with the cooking at my stockyard.

130
00:09:44,930 --> 00:09:48,520
Making mincemeat for
Abelion Sheep is no easy chore.

131
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:50,060
I would be against that...

132
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:54,860
Ulbert-<i>san</i>, don't you remember
us talking about going to get

133
00:09:54,860 --> 00:09:57,920
the rare drop from Surt, the Fire Giant Boss?

134
00:09:58,410 --> 00:10:00,950
You're the one who
doesn't remember, Touch-<i>san</i>.

135
00:10:00,950 --> 00:10:04,120
There are those here who have to
go do the Ice Dragon hunt

136
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:07,160
before they can fulfill the requirements
to change their class.

137
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:11,210
Surt's normal drop rate is lower than dragons,

138
00:10:11,210 --> 00:10:13,920
so don't you think we should
take care of that first?

139
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:17,420
Touch-<i>san</i>, I don't think
you should act so spoiled.

140
00:10:17,420 --> 00:10:20,430
No, <i>you're</i> the one who's
acting spoiled, Ulbert-<i>san</i>.

141
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:22,430
We shouldn't just be
focusing on drop rates to...

142
00:10:22,430 --> 00:10:23,930
--...I am not trying to assign blame for--

143
00:10:23,930 --> 00:10:25,560
--Shut up already!
--...I am not trying to assign blame for--

144
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:27,480
We are in the presence of Lord Ains!

145
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:30,190
Ah! Lord Ains, pardon us
for carrying on in front of you!

146
00:10:30,190 --> 00:10:32,600
I am sorry you had to
see us behave so foolishly.

147
00:10:36,470 --> 00:10:39,320
I do not mind! I forgive you. I forgive you!

148
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:42,390
That's it! We could use
a little bickering like this!

149
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:47,980
Tch, inhibited, huh?

150
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:51,830
I'd like to see this woman Tuare. Bring her here.

151
00:10:51,830 --> 00:10:55,240
Huh? Ah... Yes, as you wish!

152
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:04,080
You resemble her.

153
00:11:05,140 --> 00:11:08,730
Thanks for coming, Tuare.
I have questions for you.

154
00:11:08,730 --> 00:11:11,770
If you speak untruthfully, we are done talking,

155
00:11:11,770 --> 00:11:14,360
and if I don't get the answer I want,
we are done as well.

156
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:17,110
Now, tell me your full name.

157
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:21,360
Tuare-- Tuareninya Veyron.

158
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:27,050
You don't say. Okay, tell me, Tuareninya,

159
00:11:27,450 --> 00:11:32,760
is your desire to go to the Great Tomb
of Nazarick, and live there?

160
00:11:33,170 --> 00:11:36,550
You also have the choice of
me giving you a great deal of wealth,

161
00:11:36,550 --> 00:11:38,720
and taking it to live in a land
far away from here.

162
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:41,840
I-I would stay with Lord Sebas.

163
00:11:42,430 --> 00:11:43,800
Very well.

164
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:47,060
Listen up, my servants...

165
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:48,270
Yes, my lord!

166
00:11:48,270 --> 00:11:50,680
In the name of Ains Ooal Gown,

167
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:53,650
Tuareninya will henceforth
be under my protection!

168
00:11:53,650 --> 00:11:57,730
You may be welcomed in as my guest,
but what are your wishes?

169
00:11:57,730 --> 00:11:59,900
Th-Thank you very much,

170
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:03,660
but please, allow me
to work alongside Lord Sebas.

171
00:12:03,910 --> 00:12:06,320
If that is your desire.

172
00:12:06,870 --> 00:12:10,410
Very well, Tuareninya shall work
directly under Sebas as a provisional maid.

173
00:12:10,750 --> 00:12:14,790
At the same time, the Pleiades
will have Sebas removed as team leader,

174
00:12:14,790 --> 00:12:17,290
and with the addition of
youngest sister Aureole Omega,

175
00:12:17,290 --> 00:12:19,130
transition to become the PlÃ©iades.

176
00:12:19,130 --> 00:12:21,420
Yuri Alpha will serve as deputy leader.

177
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:25,390
Also, inform all those
in the Great Tomb of Nazarick

178
00:12:25,390 --> 00:12:29,560
that Tuareninya is under the protection
of the name of Ains Ooal Gown,

179
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:33,100
and concurrently,
will be working alongside them.

180
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:37,900
Demiurge, do you have
any objections to my decision?

181
00:12:37,900 --> 00:12:40,030
None in the least.

182
00:12:40,030 --> 00:12:43,680
Then to confirm, all of the sentries
posted in this mansion

183
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:45,660
will return to Nazarick at once.

184
00:12:46,070 --> 00:12:49,050
Sebas and Solution, prepare to withdraw.

185
00:12:49,620 --> 00:12:50,320
--Yes, my lord.
--Yes, my lord.

186
00:12:51,330 --> 00:12:53,980
--Lord Ains...
--What is it, Demiurge?

187
00:12:54,330 --> 00:12:57,840
The Abelion Sheep are omnivores,
so I would like to take this opportunity

188
00:12:57,840 --> 00:13:00,250
to procure a small amount of grain.

189
00:13:00,250 --> 00:13:01,340
I see.

190
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:05,470
Sebas, before you withdraw,
purchase a large amount of grain,

191
00:13:05,470 --> 00:13:07,340
and deliver it to Demiurge for me.

192
00:13:07,340 --> 00:13:09,060
As you wish.

193
00:13:10,930 --> 00:13:14,730
Lord Ains, did you know that girl?

194
00:13:15,270 --> 00:13:18,010
I believe it is right, you see,

195
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:21,110
to return kindness for kindness,
and evil for evil.

196
00:13:21,730 --> 00:13:24,430
That one should make sure
to pay back one's debts.

197
00:13:26,490 --> 00:13:28,450
This is the diary of...

198
00:13:29,450 --> 00:13:31,990
...a young girl whose older sister
was kidnapped by aristocrats,

199
00:13:31,990 --> 00:13:33,750
and who burned with fury inside.

200
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:39,250
This diary provided me with a general
knowledge of this world to some degree.

201
00:13:39,710 --> 00:13:41,300
Which makes me indebted to her.

202
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:44,010
I will take the debt I incurred from you,

203
00:13:44,010 --> 00:13:45,760
and pay it back to your sister.

204
00:13:48,050 --> 00:13:52,470
Lord Ains, there is one request
I would like to make of you.

205
00:13:53,350 --> 00:13:55,600
After reading the material that Sebas provided,

206
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:58,020
there is one place that I would like to go see.

207
00:13:58,020 --> 00:14:00,610
Could I impose on you for some time?

208
00:14:00,610 --> 00:14:05,110
I don't mind. You are acting for
the benefit of Nazarick, aren't you?

209
00:14:05,110 --> 00:14:07,110
Go on ahead, Demiurge.

210
00:14:07,110 --> 00:14:08,710
Thank you very much.

211
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:18,620
Solution and I are now
going to acquire some grain

212
00:14:18,620 --> 00:14:21,210
and to pay our respects to some acquaintances.

213
00:14:21,210 --> 00:14:21,920
All right...

214
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:24,920
In the meantime,
keep an eye on things here, Tuare.

215
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:28,380
Very... well... Lord Sebas...

216
00:14:29,550 --> 00:14:34,310
Last night, Climb captured the head
of Eight Fingers' slave trade division.

217
00:14:34,310 --> 00:14:36,180
Not too shabby of him.

218
00:14:36,180 --> 00:14:38,190
As such, I think we should alter our plans,

219
00:14:38,190 --> 00:14:40,400
by launching simultaneous raids today,

220
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:43,150
and taking down all of
their strongholds at once.

221
00:14:43,150 --> 00:14:46,070
If too much time passes,
it will put us at a greater disadvantage.

222
00:14:46,070 --> 00:14:50,450
Y-Yes, but Princess,
I thought we were short-handed.

223
00:14:50,450 --> 00:14:54,450
Which is why I am thinking of enlisting
the help of a nobleman I can trust.

224
00:14:54,830 --> 00:14:56,200
I have brought them.

225
00:14:57,080 --> 00:15:00,580
I am here in response to
your summons, Princess Renner.

226
00:15:00,580 --> 00:15:02,630
Yo, half-sister.

227
00:15:02,630 --> 00:15:05,840
This sounded like it would be interesting,
so I decided to attend.

228
00:15:06,210 --> 00:15:07,720
Brother?

229
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:11,140
Thank you for coming, Marquis Raeven.

230
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:13,600
I would like to ask your advice.

231
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:15,970
My advice, you say?

232
00:15:15,970 --> 00:15:19,980
I believe no one in all the court
is better versed in these matters

233
00:15:19,980 --> 00:15:21,850
than you are, Marquis Raeven.

234
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:25,900
This is bitter.

235
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:28,320
Shall I have some
fruit-infused water brought here?

236
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:31,710
Doesn't matter.
The maids who serve in the palace

237
00:15:31,710 --> 00:15:35,740
are surprisingly fast when it comes
to informing their own houses, after all.

238
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:40,000
So, what is it that you
would like to speak about?

239
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:43,210
Don't ask for too much. Even Marquis Raeven,

240
00:15:43,210 --> 00:15:46,670
one of the Six Great Nobles,
and member of the Noble Faction,

241
00:15:46,670 --> 00:15:48,380
has his position to consider.

242
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:52,050
I would like to ask you, as one who is
secretly coordinating the Royal Faction,

243
00:15:52,050 --> 00:15:55,640
if you would be able to mobilize the soldiers?

244
00:15:55,930 --> 00:15:59,270
Ordinarily, it might have been best
to first speak to the three Great Nobles

245
00:15:59,270 --> 00:16:02,060
who are connected with the Royal Faction.

246
00:16:02,060 --> 00:16:05,400
However, one of them, Marquis Blumrush,

247
00:16:05,400 --> 00:16:07,650
is feeding information to the Empire, isn't he?

248
00:16:07,650 --> 00:16:09,530
I would ask you to wait just a moment!

249
00:16:09,530 --> 00:16:13,070
You knew, right? You, who are
secretly known as the opportunist bat,

250
00:16:13,070 --> 00:16:15,410
all the while guiding both
the Royal Faction and the Noble Faction,

251
00:16:15,410 --> 00:16:18,910
acting to make sure that
the kingdom does not collapse?

252
00:16:18,910 --> 00:16:24,330
That is why you restrict things
such that little important information

253
00:16:24,330 --> 00:16:26,670
makes it to Marquis Blumrush, is it not?

254
00:16:27,090 --> 00:16:30,460
How do you, up here like
a bird in a cage, know all of that?!

255
00:16:30,460 --> 00:16:33,090
I hear a few things, and can figure it out.

256
00:16:33,090 --> 00:16:35,340
I talk to the maids, too.

257
00:16:36,220 --> 00:16:37,850
What are you, a monster?

258
00:16:39,720 --> 00:16:43,190
Understood. Let us drop all pretense.

259
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:45,220
Prince, you do not mind, do you?

260
00:16:47,190 --> 00:16:51,740
However, before we do, I would like
to speak to the real Princess Renner.

261
00:16:57,030 --> 00:16:59,280
Ah, it's better than I thought!

262
00:16:59,660 --> 00:17:02,910
Those eyes are the eyes
I saw in you as a young child!

263
00:17:03,370 --> 00:17:05,290
Have you been putting on an act?

264
00:17:06,330 --> 00:17:08,790
I had been fulfilled.

265
00:17:09,170 --> 00:17:11,550
Are you referring to Climb?

266
00:17:11,550 --> 00:17:16,870
Yes indeed. If I could be wed to Climb...
hmm, and while I'm at it,

267
00:17:16,870 --> 00:17:19,870
if I could chain him up, and keep him,
so he could not go anywhere,

268
00:17:19,870 --> 00:17:21,810
that might make me even happier.

269
00:17:21,810 --> 00:17:25,810
"Keep" him? In other words,
you are not in love with him?

270
00:17:26,190 --> 00:17:30,570
I <i>am</i> in love with him!
I very much like his eyes!

271
00:17:30,570 --> 00:17:34,450
I also love the way
he follows me around, like a dog.

272
00:17:34,450 --> 00:17:36,910
Sorry, but I'm not following at all.

273
00:17:36,910 --> 00:17:39,660
I am not asking you to understand.

274
00:17:39,660 --> 00:17:44,910
As long as you know that I am fond of him,
and that I love him, that is enough.

275
00:17:44,910 --> 00:17:48,920
However, marrying a commoner such as...
M-Master Climb might be...

276
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:53,260
Can't we strike a deal? Once I accede
to the throne, I'll hitch you and Climb.

277
00:17:53,260 --> 00:17:55,170
--Count me in!
--That was fast!

278
00:17:55,170 --> 00:17:59,890
From the moment you arrived, Brother,
I wanted to bring that subject up.

279
00:17:59,890 --> 00:18:03,680
I also have a request for you, Marquis Raeven.

280
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:04,930
What might that be?

281
00:18:04,930 --> 00:18:07,940
Marquis Raeven, you have a son, yes?

282
00:18:07,940 --> 00:18:09,690
Yes, he is still only five.

283
00:18:10,020 --> 00:18:12,190
I ask that he be my betrothed.

284
00:18:12,490 --> 00:18:13,190
No!

285
00:18:13,190 --> 00:18:17,000
You think I would give my boy
to a woman like you?!

286
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:22,700
P-Pardon me, Your Highnesses.

287
00:18:23,910 --> 00:18:25,950
Would you mind telling me your reasons?

288
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:28,460
I am sure you already know.

289
00:18:29,170 --> 00:18:33,380
Your Highness would marry my son,
but have children with Climb.

290
00:18:33,380 --> 00:18:36,470
My son would bear children
with whichever woman he loved,

291
00:18:36,470 --> 00:18:39,640
which you could then claim
as your successors. Does that sum it up?

292
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:42,220
Are you really proposing this
right in front of me?

293
00:18:42,220 --> 00:18:44,720
Ah, you would not want
to learn of it later, would you?

294
00:18:46,730 --> 00:18:49,650
So, I hear you are
going up against Eight Fingers?

295
00:18:49,650 --> 00:18:53,730
Yes. I would like to strike at them
before they burrow underground,

296
00:18:53,730 --> 00:18:54,860
but I am short of soldiers.

297
00:18:54,860 --> 00:18:56,490
Where will you be attacking?

298
00:18:57,110 --> 00:18:58,400
These seven locations.

299
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:00,990
The problem is that each of these locations

300
00:19:00,990 --> 00:19:03,120
is in a territory owned by a different nobleman.

301
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:06,160
If we could just uncover something
that ties them with Eight Fingers,

302
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:09,080
I could use it to exert pressure on the nobles.

303
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:11,630
Barring that, we can just find something, right?

304
00:19:11,630 --> 00:19:14,420
It's definite where they dispose
of their incriminating materials.

305
00:19:14,420 --> 00:19:18,170
Also, my sister, I have an important question.

306
00:19:18,170 --> 00:19:21,550
Our beloved older brother, the first prince,

307
00:19:21,550 --> 00:19:24,010
is also taking money from Eight Fingers, right?

308
00:19:24,010 --> 00:19:26,180
Ah, Brother Barbro?

309
00:19:26,180 --> 00:19:28,930
This would be the
perfect evidence to depose him.

310
00:19:28,930 --> 00:19:33,690
I'd like to include the drug division
stronghold he deals with in your plans.

311
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:37,320
Then that will make eight places for us to raid.

312
00:19:37,320 --> 00:19:41,740
As far as manpower, I will send my own
guardsmen and the factions' soldiers.

313
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:43,990
However, while we may have enough numbers,

314
00:19:43,990 --> 00:19:46,040
whether we can go up against Six Arms,

315
00:19:46,040 --> 00:19:48,580
which is said to be
adamantite class, is the question.

316
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:51,740
I have a request in
at the adventurer's guild, too.

317
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:54,190
He's here.

318
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:59,690
This is a gentleman who may help us.

319
00:20:04,090 --> 00:20:08,220
That took a bit of time, but we did
finish arrangements to transport the grain,

320
00:20:08,220 --> 00:20:11,230
so now we can return
to Nazarick without any issues.

321
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:14,120
Tuare! Tuare, are you here?!

322
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:22,200
There are a number of fresh marks
around the front door's keyhole.

323
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:25,770
I believe there is a good chance
that someone picked the lock.

324
00:20:27,020 --> 00:20:30,410
Tuare has been kidnapped,
which means that I am going to rescue her.

325
00:20:30,410 --> 00:20:34,000
A time and place have been
carefully spelled out here.

326
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,500
I wonder if that is the best course.

327
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:40,460
I just mean that before you go,
we should inform Lord Ains.

328
00:20:40,460 --> 00:20:44,010
Lord Sebas, have you
forgotten his words earlier?

329
00:20:45,220 --> 00:20:48,470
Report this to Lord Ains.
Tell him that Tuare has been kidnapped,

330
00:20:48,470 --> 00:20:50,300
and ask what we should do about it.

331
00:20:55,230 --> 00:20:56,310
Albedo...

332
00:20:56,310 --> 00:21:00,070
Y-Yes, Lord Ains? Is something the matter?

333
00:21:00,070 --> 00:21:04,700
I just got a message from Sebas--
or rather, Solution--

334
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:08,160
and apparently, the woman that
Sebas took in, Tuare, has been abducted.

335
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:10,080
I am otherwise occupied at the moment.

336
00:21:10,080 --> 00:21:12,700
I need you to put together
some forces to back Sebas up.

337
00:21:13,290 --> 00:21:17,580
Lord Ains, please permit me
the folly of raising an objection,

338
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:22,970
but is there any value in saving
an inferior creature such as a human?

339
00:21:23,260 --> 00:21:27,760
Albedo, I promised to save Tuareninya

340
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:31,810
in the name of Ains Ooal Gown. Is that clear?

341
00:21:31,810 --> 00:21:36,440
Is that clear?! I promised her
my protection, in my name, no less!

342
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:39,860
Even if they did not know,
this cannot be allowed to stand!

343
00:21:40,690 --> 00:21:41,780
Sorry.

344
00:21:41,780 --> 00:21:45,740
There is nothing for which
you need to apologize, Lord Ains!

345
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:49,030
Your order is received.
In addition to rescuing her,

346
00:21:49,030 --> 00:21:53,080
I will see that the hammer falls on
those lowly humans who have upset you!

347
00:21:53,080 --> 00:21:58,560
Tell you what. You organize them,
and Demiurge will command them onsite.

348
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:03,620
Still, I don't understand.

349
00:22:04,170 --> 00:22:06,380
Ains Ooal Gown...

350
00:22:08,680 --> 00:22:09,650
This is ridiculous.

351
00:22:09,650 --> 00:22:11,650


